  rail_buffer_stop) prompts=(
    "Line end railway tile: a single regular hexagonal diorama tile with exactly six straight flat edges, centred in frame, 32 m across, lush meadow grass cap and $skirt, flat-topped so one flat side faces the camera along the bottom of the frame, carrying a $rail. Seen from above, the track runs straight from the middle of the bottom side across the centre of the tile and ends just inside the middle of the top side at a traditional country railway buffer stop standing square across the track at the very end of the rails: a stout horizontal timber buffer beam painted bright red, two round sprung buffers with dark grey steel heads on its face looking back down the track, a small round red lamp on top of the beam, carried on a sturdy frame of old steel rails bent up from the running rails. The rest of the tile is open meadow grass, $toprail"
