    "A single flat-sided hexagonal diorama tile, 32 m across, lush meadow grass cap and $skirt. An 8 m wide river runs straight between two opposite flat edges in a channel sunk below the meadow surface between natural earthy banks with pebbles and reeds, $water. Close to one bank floats one $rowboat, about 3.5 m long, so the boat is less than half the river's width and small against the tile, tied by a single rope to a short weathered timber landing stage of a few planks on posts at the water's edge. Where the river reaches the tile side wall, $cut, $style"
