    "A single regular hexagonal deep ocean tile for a diorama with exactly six straight flat edges and six corners, centred in frame, 32 m across, flat-topped so one flat side faces the camera along the bottom of the frame, on a plain neutral grey studio backdrop. Open temperate sea with layered gentle waves, a few white foam flecks on crests, $water. On every side $cut. Near the middle of the tile sails one $sailboat, about 5 m long with its mast about 6 m tall, so the hull is only about one sixth of the tile's width and the boat looks small against the open sea around it, its sail filled and the hull heeling slightly, with a short white foam wake trailing from its stern. Through the clear side walls a darker sandy seabed with scattered pebbles shows below. Stylized-real diorama miniature, real PBR materials, slightly exaggerated proportions, soft noon sun, neutral grey studio background, high camera looking down at about 65 degrees elevation so all six hexagon edges read clearly") ;;
  lighthouse) tower="a round gently tapering stone lighthouse tower about 20 m tall painted in broad horizontal bands of white and bright red, a plain timber door at its foot, small plain square windows up the tower, a black iron gallery with a railing near the top, a round glazed lamp room above the gallery with a grid of slender black glazing bars around a large faceted glass lens, and a domed black cap with a small ball finial"
