    "Close-up of the top of a lighthouse on a diorama tile: the white and bright red banded tower top, the black iron gallery with a railing on stone brackets, the round glazed lamp room with a grid of slender black glazing bars, a large faceted glass lens inside around a warm lamp, and a domed black cap with a ball finial and a slim lightning rod, every surface plain and unmarked, $style"
    "Lighthouse coast tile at dusk: a single flat-sided hexagonal coast tile for a diorama, 32 m across. Ocean fills the side with two adjacent flat edges, $water, with a lacy white surf foam line against a low rocky headland of weathered grey granite topped with lush meadow grass, on which stands $tower, beside $keeper. The lamp is lit, and one soft warm-white beam of light shines out of the lamp room level across the sea toward one side, fading with distance, while the cottage windows glow warm yellow. Under the land, $skirt. On the ocean side, $cut. Stylized-real diorama miniature, real PBR materials, slightly exaggerated proportions, deep blue dusk light with a last warm orange glow low on one side, dark blue-grey studio background, 35 degree three-quarter view") ;;
  # Village well (owner 2026-10-20): the cottage kit's materials (house_cluster ref-1, $cottage): grey
